title: Slack agent lacks native task execution UX and thread lifecycle
updated_at: "2026-11-02T06:19:38Z"
---
Research found Slack's agent UX supports more than a plain reply: start/update task progress in the originating thread, surface processing/loading and stop controls, preserve a stable per-thread session so follow-up mentions continue the same work, and post completion summaries/actions in-thread. Claude Tag and Slack agent guidance also emphasize context from the full thread and visible async progress. Clawq should use Slack's supported agent/thread UX for execution runs and when tagged in threads, rather than treating each mention as an isolated chat response. Investigate supported Slack APIs/scopes and implement the appropriate experience while preserving channel access boundaries and guest/privacy controls. References: https://support.claude.com/en/articles/15594475-what-is-claude-tag ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/slack ; https://docs.slack.dev/ai/developing-agents/ ; https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/agents_api/apps/slack_bot/readme

Decision (2026-11-02 batch): same Slack worktree after B835 and B832. Verified Slack currently derives reply/thread handling separately and lacks native assistant task lifecycle. Use documented assistant/thread APIs with stable per-thread identity, full authorized thread context, processing/progress/final cleanup and stop handling; preserve guest/channel authorization.

Decision (primary-source research 2026-11-02): Current Slack docs distinguish default agent_view from legacy assistant_view. Implement the selected experience explicitly; agents.sessions.setStatus/rename plus agent_session_stopped support native stop with chat:write. Legacy assistant_thread_* events alone do not cover current agent_view. Stable thread identity, authorized full-thread context, matching-run cancellation and terminal status cleanup remain required; source URLs captured in Slack research receipt.

Schema decision2026-11-02: exact official agents.sessions methods use channel_id+root thread_ts, not a native session/run ID; agent_session_stopped has channel/thread/user/event_ts and optional-empty streaming_message_ts array, with no per-run cancellation token. Correlate native stops with app-owned live stream/run state; do not interrupt whichever run happens to be current. Use run-specific public BlockKit controls for queued/nonstreaming/fallback cases and handle ambiguous empty-stream stops conservatively with disclosed limits. Standalone app_context_changed has no documented reliable actor/thread locator: context is untrusted data, never an access grant or fanout instruction. Receipt B833-api-schema-receipt.md supplements primary-source research; implementation remains after B832 review gate.

Implementation integration requirement2026-11-02: durable per-thread routing must preserve the real channel identity for room authorization/profile selection, including model/instructions/template/CWD/tool policy and reloads. Parent source trace found the new thread key would otherwise miss existing full-key/channel profile matching despite snapshot room access. Add production bound-profile regression and preserve exact-binding precedence with room fallback, avoiding module dependency cycles. Also require fail-closed unknown private metadata/shared-room policy parity and generation-safe delayed status cleanup; include deterministic mocked tests before review. Persisted resume/background/notifier-loss deliveries must return to originating root thread.

Independent security review2026-11-02 FAIL on 0a54d394: accepted S1 exact-thread access snapshot/egress collapses to parent permissions; S2 persisted fallback and origin-bearing room progress can send with stale config or omit current egress; S3 durable queued Slack followups/restart drainer execute without preserved requester provenance and fresh authorization; S4 retained status edit/delete callbacks use old credentials. Fix all in one bounded tests-first round after independent lifecycle review; preserve actual channel room IDs, B832 injected-caller isolation and B831 held/canonical recovery. Missing replay provenance must refuse/hold rather than invent authority. No merge or closure until independent rereviews pass; all builds/tests on x-p35.